[h1]Bardstown, Kentucky (Town)[/h1]
An unofficial, fan-made Build 42 map of the real town of Bardstown, Kentucky, built from OpenStreetMap data. It is free.

The streets are real and carry their real names. Shops, churches, schools and a museum sit where OpenStreetMap puts them, and homes are game buildings on real plots. Loot spawns the way the game normally does it: in testing, the pharmacy had pills and the grocery fridges had food. The in-game map shows the real street names and landmarks.

It covers up to a 3 km square, clipped to Bardstown's city limits: 169 map cells, about 185 MB.

[h2]How to play[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Subscribe, then enable [b]Bardstown, Kentucky (Town)[/b] under [b]Mods[/b].
[*]Start a [b]New Game[/b] and pick Bardstown from the spawn region list, next to the vanilla towns. You start in a home near downtown.
[*]A map can only be added to a new world. It will not show up in a save you already have.
[/olist]
Back up your saves before trying any map mod.

Enable only one Portal or KnoxMap town at a time: they are all placed at the same spot in the world, so two at once would overlap.

What has been tested: singleplayer on one Windows PC. Multiplayer has not been tested. Please report anything that breaks in the comments.

KnoxMap is designed to work with two optional mods, Elevators (lifts in taller buildings) and Spawn Selector (pick your spawn spot). Neither has been tested with this map yet. Both are separate mods by their own authors.

[h2]Make your own town with Portal[/h2]
Optional: the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3833266816]Portal companion mod[/url] adds a PORTAL entry to the main menu that lists your Portal towns and explains how to make your own. More towns: the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3833268857]Portal collection[/url].

Portal is a free, unofficial Windows app. You search for a real place, pick a size, and press Generate & Play, and it builds a map mod like this one. Results depend on how well the place is mapped in OpenStreetMap, larger sizes take a long time and need a strong PC, and so far only a few towns have been tried.

Download and source: [url=https://github.com/derpasaurus69-crypto/zomboidmods/releases]https://github.com/derpasaurus69-crypto/zomboidmods/releases[/url]

Portal is a front end for [url=https://github.com/spytheeuclidean-a11y/knoxmap]KnoxMap[/url] by euclid80tr, which does the real work of turning map data into a furnished, compiled PZ map. KnoxMap is built on Knoxify by arytek. Portal does not include KnoxMap; you install it separately.

[h2]Real places[/h2]
This is a real town. The streets, place names and public buildings come from OpenStreetMap, which anyone can view. Building interiors, residents and zombies are invented by the generator and do not describe the real places or anyone connected with them. If you live in Bardstown and something here bothers you, leave a comment and I will look at it.

